Month = {MAR 15},
Abstract = {Using ANSYS FLUENT numerical modeling and mathematical modeling, the
   main characteristics of combustion processes during the combustion of
   natural gas were determined. In this work, the combustion processes and
   NO x formation in the firebox were modeled at different loads of the GM-
   50-14/250 boiler. The temperature distribution along the height of the
   firebox and the heat load on the screen panels were determined. The
   results of calculations by two types of models were compared with each
   other and with the data of measurements on the operating equipment. The
   environmental performance of the firebox, namely the formation of NO x
   at different heat loads, was determined. The maximum boiler capacity at
   which its operation meets European environmental standards was
   determined. The deviation of calculations on the formation of NO x in
   the GM -50-14/250 boiler at 40\% of the rated power compared to the
   results of field tests using ANSYS FLUENT modeling was 8\%, and using
   the mathematical model - 27\%. When operating at rated power, the
   deviations of the results decreased to 2\% and 8\%, respectively. The
   deviation of the results of thermal calculations of the combustion in
   the firebox by different types of modeling in the active combustion zone
   and at the outlet of the firebox is up to 3\% at different loads.},
